{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwbiYps3qhMxDFZaFeTC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard to look at the panels, and I haven't seen the rule run.\n\n**Data:** The logs have a `timestamp` field and fields for the response code, bytes, file extension, source and destination geography, client IP, host, machine OS and agent. `response` is a string field, so I filter and group on `response.keyword`.\n\n**Dashboard** \"EFF-650313bb Web logs overview\" (id `eff-650313bb-web-logs-overview-a079c3529ac7`) has five panels over the last 7 days:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Requests by response code\n- Average bytes by file extension\n- Top source countries\n\nThe dashboard is at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-650313bb-web-logs-overview-a079c3529ac7.\n\n**Rule** \"EFF-650313bb 5xx spike\" (id `77f2f203-d51f-4f2f-aa87-f2640fec3755`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and counts documents matching `response.keyword: 5*` in the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10. It has no action attached, so it will show up as an alert in Kibana but won't send a notification anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":20429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"output_tokens":448,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"829ba4d0-4780-406d-b1dc-e7dea9fef8b3","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:02:47.751Z","request_id":"req_011CfwbiYbi6PURUyQ3GauLw"}
